(OPR-42 (undocumented precision): a text, buffer or list operand in a
 BITWISE expression is a compile error, the same as in arithmetic.
 LANGUAGE.md:1865 states this for arithmetic only; the Operators
 section says nothing about the bitwise operators' domain, and the
 bitwise table sits 2700 lines away from that note. Memory safety is
 preserved by the compiler, not by luck - this is the row that says so.
 Contrast OPR-38: a FLOAT operand is silently accepted and gives 0.0.
 (Compile-error claim: not assertable from a runtime leaf.)
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox OPR-42.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Cannot use text label in arithmetic; cast it first with 'as a number' or 'as a float'.
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a text called label is "hello".
Print label bit-and 1.
